 ;; IM3 — Integrated Math III
 {:course/id #uuid "8c5a7faa-f162-501c-8c6f-43b7cf6e6619"
  :course/math-academy-id 134
  :course/title "Integrated Math III"
  :course/code "IM3"
  :course/level :course.level/high-school-math
  :course/description "Our fully accredited Common Core-aligned Integrated Math III course builds upon the strong foundations formed in Integrated Math I and Integrated Math II , further developing students' knowledge and skills in polynomials, rationals, radicals, exponentials, logarithms, number systems, geometry, trigonometry, and probability. Upon completing this course, students will attain the knowledge and skills needed to study Precalculus ."
  :course/overview "As part of this comprehensive course, students generalize their knowledge of quadratics to higher-order polynomials. This includes factoring polynomials using various methods, solving polynomial equations, and dividing polynomials. Students will also grasp fundamental polynomial theorems, such as the factor and remainder theorems, learn how to plot polynomials and describe their properties.\nStudents will learn to solve exponential and logarithmic equations and further develop their aptitude for modeling scenarios with exponential functions, such as calculating compound interest. Additionally, they will develop fluency in radical and rational expressions and equations, including manipulating and simplifying expressions, solving equations, and plotting graphs.\nBuilding upon the foundations laid in Integrated Math II , students will strengthen their knowledge of arithmetic and geometric sequences. They'll also explore the properties of the real number system and use their knowledge of quadratics as a stepping stone to investigate the complex numbers.\nStudents deepen their knowledge of geometry, including proof, circles, and parabolas in the coordinate plane. They will further develop their understanding of trigonometry, including the law of sines and cosines, graphs, and properties of trigonometric functions."
