  :course/title "AP Calculus AB"
  :course/code "CAB"
  :course/level :course.level/university-math
  :course/description "Our accredited AP Calculus AB course is aligned with the College Board's AP Calculus AB specification. By completing this course, students will acquire a solid grasp of the essential concepts necessary for success on the AP exam. In addition, students will gain a concrete foundation to progress to advanced study in other STEM-related disciplines."
  :course/overview "This course is designed to provide students with a strong foundation in single-variable calculus, equipping them with the necessary knowledge and skills to excel in higher-level mathematics. This comprehensive course covers essential topics such as limits, continuity differentiation, integration, differential equations, and various applications of single-variable calculus."
  :course/outcomes [
    {:course-outcome/id #uuid "53369700-2cee-5802-83a6-b8b7aab32974"
     :course-outcome/index 1
     :course-outcome/text "Understand and analyze limits and continuity, including estimating limits from graphs, the algebra of limits, limits of functions, determining limits using algebraic manipulation, and special limits."
     :db/ensure :course-outcome/validate}
    {:course-outcome/id #uuid "c9aec01c-168f-5fa3-a4c0-311030a6f3b5"
     :course-outcome/index 2
     :course-outcome/text "Understand continuity, including defining continuity at a point, classifying discontinuities, removing discontinuities, and the intermediate value theorem."
     :db/ensure :course-outcome/validate}
