    {:course-outcome/id #uuid "e17362d4-ba2f-5103-abd6-fe6e9140af0b"
     :course-outcome/index 1
     :course-outcome/text "Master the concept of limits, including estimating limits from graphs, the algebra of limits, limits of functions, determining limits using algebraic manipulation, and special limits involving trigonometric functions."
     :db/ensure :course-outcome/validate}
    {:course-outcome/id #uuid "fad36616-e00d-5880-9af0-963885ec6f35"
     :course-outcome/index 2
     :course-outcome/text "Understand continuity, including defining continuity at a point, classifying discontinuities, removing discontinuities, and the intermediate value theorem."
     :db/ensure :course-outcome/validate}
    {:course-outcome/id #uuid "75ec7cdb-3f27-518b-8aff-eee6069163e3"
     :course-outcome/index 3
     :course-outcome/text "Learn the basics of differentiation, including instantaneous rates of change, calculating derivatives using the definition, the rules of differentiation, differentiating exponential, logarithmic, trigonometric, and inverse trigonometric functions, computing tangent and normal lines, the chain rule, implicit differentiation, and differentiating inverse functions."
     :db/ensure :course-outcome/validate}
    {:course-outcome/id #uuid "9c93ed7b-611e-5ef9-8a5c-7807d5e49e84"
     :course-outcome/index 4
     :course-outcome/text "Explore contextual applications of differentiation, including interpreting the meaning of the derivative in context, estimating derivatives, related rates of change, and L'Hopital's Rule."
